00:09:00,430 --> 00:09:05,120
DeepSeek starts checking the connection, looks through the available tools, and gives us a report.

142
00:09:05,678 --> 00:09:10,320
It even opens a local system file to check whether REA can actually inspect something.

143
00:09:10,894 --> 00:09:11,920
And it works perfectly!

144
00:09:12,622 --> 00:09:19,900
Now, before moving forward, we need to pay attention to a few additional tools, including Hopper, but the main connection is working.

145
00:09:20,494 --> 00:09:25,240
So we've got our AI developer talking to REA, and both are connected through OpenRouter.

146
00:09:25,678 --> 00:09:26,440
Pretty cool, right?

147
00:09:27,022 --> 00:09:32,840
But there's one more thing I want to show you, and this is actually one of the most useful parts of this entire setup.

148
00:09:33,550 --> 00:09:36,388
See, free AI models usually come with limits.

149
00:09:37,020 --> 00:09:41,660
Imagine you're halfway through building an app, and suddenly the model you're using reaches its limit.

150
00:09:41,838 --> 00:09:47,040
Now you have to switch to another model, reconnect everything, and figure out where you left off.

151
00:09:47,502 --> 00:09:49,360
That's exactly what we want to avoid.

152
00:09:49,934 --> 00:09:56,020
So instead of relying on one model, we're going to create a small team of free models that can back each other up.

153
00:09:56,430 --> 00:09:58,740
And for that, we'll use OpenRouter's presets.

154
00:09:59,534 --> 00:10:01,640
Think of a preset as a saved setup.

155
00:10:02,126 --> 00:10:07,000
We choose the models once, save everything together, and connect that setup to DeepSeek Harness.

156
00:10:07,758 --> 00:10:11,940
So head back to OpenRouter, open Presets, and click New Preset.

157
00:10:12,334 --> 00:10:20,140
I'm going to name ours Free Models and in the description I'll write Free AI Model Fallback for DeepSeek plus Rhea.

158
00:10:20,750 --> 00:10:23,580
Now scroll down to Models and click Add Model.

159
00:10:24,120 --> 00:10:27,720
First we're adding NVIDIA NEMOTRON 3 Ultra, Free.

160
00:10:28,260 --> 00:10:32,680
Next NVIDIA NEMOTRON 3.5 Super VL, Free.

161
00:10:33,134 --> 00:10:37,260
And finally NVIDIA NEMOTRON 3.5 lightning free.

162
00:10:37,870 --> 00:10:41,060
So now we've got three free AI models in one place.

163
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:42,852
And here's why we're doing this.

164
00:10:43,374 --> 00:10:46,300
Think of it like having three people working on the same project.

165
00:10:46,670 --> 00:10:49,460
If one person can't continue, another can step in.

166
00:10:49,838 --> 00:10:51,140
It's a similar idea here.

167
00:10:51,534 --> 00:10:59,780
With model fallback configured, if one model becomes unavailable or hits a supported usage limit, Open Router can try another model from our list.

168
00:11:00,238 --> 00:11:04,980
That means we don't have to manually change our model settings every single time something goes wrong.

169
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:12,000
Of course, this still depends on the available free models and their limits, but it makes the whole setup a lot more flexible.

170
00:11:12,600 --> 00:11:14,720
Now, scroll down to the Tools section.

171
00:11:15,260 --> 00:11:20,800
Here we'll enable Web Search, Date Time, Fusion, Advisor, and Subagent.

172
00:11:21,230 --> 00:11:23,600
Once that's done, click Save Preset.

173
00:11:24,080 --> 00:11:29,620
And OpenRouter gives us a preset ID, at preset slash free dash models.

174
00:11:30,160 --> 00:11:32,860
Copy this, because we're going to connect it to DeepSeek Harness.

175
00:11:32,860 --> 00:11:36,960
Now head back to Harness, open Settings, and go to Models.

176
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:40,940
Under our OpenRouterFreeProvider, click Add Model.

177
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:49,500
Paste at preset-free-models into the Model ID field, give it the display name FreeModels, and click Apply.

178
00:11:50,062 --> 00:11:50,760
And that's it!

179
00:11:51,150 --> 00:11:54,020
We've connected our custom model setup to DeepSeek Harness.

180
00:11:54,734 --> 00:12:02,820
So now, instead of depending on just one AI model, our developer has a list of models it can use, with fallback options if one isn't available.

181
00:12:03,406 --> 00:12:05,760
And that's what makes this setup so useful.

182
00:12:06,350 --> 00:12:08,980
Now, let's quickly look at everything we've done so far.

183
00:12:09,486 --> 00:12:18,980
We've set up DeepSeek Harness as our AI developer, connected REA to help it understand other apps, and added OpenRouter to power everything with free AI models.

184
00:12:19,598 --> 00:12:25,740
So now, we've got our developer, the right tools, and the AI models, all without needing a paid subscription.

